meta {
  name: 04a2 - Get Mapping (with Strategies)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/biprws/raylight/v1/documents/{{docId}}/dataproviders/mappings?originDataproviderIds={{originDataproviderIds}}&targetDatasourceId={{targetDsId}}&skipChecking=false
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  X-SAP-LogonToken: {{logonToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  docId: 5418
  originDataproviderIds: DP0
  targetDsId: 5406
}

body:json {
  {
    "strategies": {
      "strategy": [
        { "name": "SamePath", "enabled": true },
        { "name": "SameTechnicalName", "enabled": true },
        { "name": "SameName", "enabled": true },
        { "name": "Removal", "enabled": false }
      ]
    }
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // Store the strategy-driven mapping so 04b can POST it back to APPLY the change.
  if (res.getStatus() === 200 && res.getBody()) {
    bru.setEnvVar("mappingPayload", JSON.stringify(res.getBody()));
    console.log("mappingPayload (strategy-driven) stored.");
  } else {
    console.log("Strategy mapping failed: status " + res.getStatus());
  }
}

docs {
  STRATEGY-DRIVEN MAPPING — computes the object mapping using strategies YOU
  control (safer alternative to 04a's default GET).

  VERIFIED LIVE against this server:
    GET  .../mappings?...            -> 200  (compute with default strategies)
    GET  .../mappings?...  + body    -> 200  (compute with YOUR strategies)  << THIS
    POST .../mappings?...  + strategies body -> 400 WSR 00103 (NOT allowed)

  So the `strategies` body must be sent on the **GET** (compute) request — NOT
  on POST. The POST verb is reserved for APPLYING an already-computed mapping
  (that's what 04b does, posting the mapping payload — no `strategies` element).

  STRATEGIES:
    SamePath / SameTechnicalName / SameName  -> how objects are matched
    Removal (disabled)                       -> KEEP unmatched objects (don't
                                                delete report objects)

  NOTE: when the source & target universes share identical object ids, the
  mapping comes back all "Ok" regardless of strategies. Strategies matter when
  ids / names differ between universes.

  FLOW:
    1. 04a2 (THIS)  -> GET + strategies  => strategy-driven mapping, stored in
                       env var `mappingPayload`.
    2. 04b          -> POST `mappingPayload` back to the SAME url => APPLIES it.
    3. 05           -> PUT documents/{docId} (empty body) => SAVE.
    4. 06 / 07      -> close session / logoff.
}

tests {
  test("Strategy mapping retrieved", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}